    "claim_id": "SCOPED-ODD-TORSION-TRANSLATION",
    "claim": "For any type A with associative commutative addition and a two-sided zero,\ndefine multiple r P by repeated addition. Let P,T:A and r:Nat. Suppose\nthere exists k:Nat with r=k+k+1, multiple r P=zero, T+T=zero and T!=zero.\nThen multiple r (P+T)!=zero. More precisely multiple r (P+T)=T.\nNo concrete curve, factor base, or subgroup membership certificate is imported.",
